Why this is here
----------------

An InDesign plugin cannot be built without the Adobe InDesign SDK, and the
resulting binary is not merely linked against it. Adobe ships the plugin entry
point, the plugin's statics, and the precompiled-header source as *source*,
and every plugin compiles that source into itself. Both StrokeMaster plugins,
the engine (InDesignStrokeEngine.pln) and the panel (StrokeMasterUI.pln),
compile these three of Adobe's files:

    SDKPlugInEntrypoint.cpp  PlugInStatics.cpp  VCPlugInHeaders.cpp

and link the SDK's libraries. Each of those files carries Adobe's copyright and
a license permitting use only "in accordance with the terms of the Adobe
license agreement accompanying it." That is a restriction GPL section 10
forbids anyone from imposing on a recipient, and section 5(c) requires the
whole combined work to be licensed under the GPL, which no one but Adobe is in
a position to do for Adobe's code.

So the source in this repository is unambiguously GPL: it contains no Adobe
code, and the SDK is referenced by path rather than vendored. The *compiled
plugins* would not be distributable under a bare GPL, because the license they
purported to grant would cover code the copyright holder has no authority to
relicense. Section 7 exists for exactly this situation, and this file uses it.

